In the present case, as referred above, there are serious charges against applicant that he committed offence of attempt to rape on a minor girl.
Statement of victim recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C. is specific in this regard.
There is merit in the argument of learned AGA that applicant belongs to same village, therefore,
there is likelihood that in case of bail, he may try to influence victim and other witnesses.
